1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,652
March 13, 1962.

2
00:00:02,992 --> 00:00:05,071
A memo leaves the Joint Chiefs of Staff,

3
00:00:05,091 --> 00:00:07,065
addressed to the Secretary of Defense.

4
00:00:07,635 --> 00:00:09,351
Its subject line is dry.

5
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:11,956
Justification for U.S. military

6
00:00:11,976 --> 00:00:13,340
intervention in Cuba.

7
00:00:13,909 --> 00:00:16,158
Inside is a list of staged incidents.

8
00:00:16,741 --> 00:00:18,936
A fake attack on an American base.

9
00:00:19,519 --> 00:00:21,682
A ship blown up, and blamed on Cuba.

10
00:00:22,265 --> 00:00:24,403
A passenger plane that would only appear

11
00:00:24,423 --> 00:00:25,266
to be shot down.

12
00:00:25,836 --> 00:00:27,820
It was signed by the highest-ranking

13
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:29,434
officer in the U.S. military.

14
00:00:30,254 --> 00:00:31,986
It stayed secret for decades.

15
00:00:32,326 --> 00:00:34,559
Today, it's quoted all over the internet.

16
00:00:35,029 --> 00:00:36,654
So what does it actually say?

17
00:00:37,124 --> 00:00:38,253
And what happened to it?

18
00:00:38,823 --> 00:00:40,096
Let's open the file.

19
00:00:46,423 --> 00:00:48,255
To understand the memo, start a year

20
00:00:48,275 --> 00:00:48,667
earlier.

21
00:00:49,287 --> 00:00:52,098
In April 1961, a CIA-trained force of

22
00:00:52,118 --> 00:00:55,083
Cuban exiles landed at the Bay of Pigs.

23
00:00:55,423 --> 00:00:57,853
Fidel Castro's forces defeated it quickly.

24
00:00:58,423 --> 00:01:00,533
The defeat left a mark in Washington.

25
00:01:00,873 --> 00:01:02,936
According to the Joint Chiefs' official

26
00:01:02,956 --> 00:01:04,965
biography of their chairman, President

27
00:01:04,985 --> 00:01:07,101
Kennedy felt the Chiefs had not reviewed

28
00:01:07,121 --> 00:01:09,024
the plan thoroughly, or voiced their

29
00:01:09,044 --> 00:01:10,413
reservations forthrightly.

30
00:01:10,983 --> 00:01:13,589
By early 1962, there was a new, secret

31
00:01:13,609 --> 00:01:15,179
program against Castro.

32
00:01:15,519 --> 00:01:17,410
It was called Operation Mongoose.

33
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:20,305
Its chief of operations was an Air Force

34
00:01:20,325 --> 00:01:21,770
general, Edward Lansdale.

35
00:01:22,110 --> 00:01:24,167
In February, he put the goal on paper.

36
00:01:24,737 --> 00:01:27,197
The United States would help the people of

37
00:01:27,217 --> 00:01:29,617
Cuba overthrow the Communist regime, from

38
00:01:29,637 --> 00:01:30,325
within Cuba.

39
00:01:30,895 --> 00:01:33,898
His schedule aimed for an open revolt in

40
00:01:33,918 --> 00:01:35,485
Cuba by October 1962.

41
00:01:35,955 --> 00:01:37,916
But it left one big question open.

42
00:01:38,256 --> 00:01:40,706
If a revolt began, would the U.S. military

43
00:01:40,726 --> 00:01:41,177
step in?

44
00:01:41,747 --> 00:01:43,883
On March 5, Lansdale's office asked the

45
00:01:43,903 --> 00:01:45,873
Joint Chiefs for something specific.

46
00:01:46,213 --> 00:01:48,284
A brief but precise description of

47
00:01:48,304 --> 00:01:50,867
pretexts, that would justify U.S. military

48
00:01:50,887 --> 00:01:52,158
intervention in Cuba.

49
00:01:52,729 --> 00:01:54,876
And according to a footnote in the file,

50
00:01:54,896 --> 00:01:56,773
three days later the Chief of Naval

51
00:01:56,793 --> 00:01:59,049
Operations sent the Chairman a memo of his

52
00:01:59,069 --> 00:01:59,266
own.

53
00:01:59,606 --> 00:02:02,071
Its title: Instances to Provoke Military

54
00:02:02,091 --> 00:02:03,066
Actions in Cuba.

55
00:02:03,885 --> 00:02:05,553
The Joint Chiefs answered fast.

56
00:02:06,173 --> 00:02:08,512
On March 13, the Chairman of the Joint

57
00:02:08,532 --> 00:02:11,057
Chiefs, General Lyman Lemnitzer, signed a

58
00:02:11,077 --> 00:02:13,415
cover memo to Defense Secretary Robert

59
00:02:13,435 --> 00:02:13,974
McNamara.

60
00:02:14,544 --> 00:02:17,000
Behind it sat a staff report, and an annex

61
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:19,122
with a title that leaves no room for

62
00:02:19,142 --> 00:02:19,476
doubt.

63
00:02:19,896 --> 00:02:22,119
Pretexts to justify U.S. military

64
00:02:22,139 --> 00:02:23,547
intervention in Cuba.

65
00:02:24,117 --> 00:02:25,951
In the Joint Staff's paperwork, the

66
00:02:25,971 --> 00:02:27,433
subject carried a code word.

67
00:02:28,015 --> 00:02:28,835
Northwoods.

68
00:02:29,755 --> 00:02:31,903
The Chiefs called the list a preliminary

69
00:02:31,923 --> 00:02:33,692
submission, suitable for planning

70
00:02:33,712 --> 00:02:34,180
purposes.

71
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:36,594
Individual projects, they wrote, could be

72
00:02:36,614 --> 00:02:37,820
considered case by case.

73
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:39,930
They also asked for a role.

74
00:02:40,270 --> 00:02:42,609
Responsibility for both overt and covert

75
00:02:42,629 --> 00:02:44,850
military operations, they recommended,

76
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:46,620
should go to the Joint Chiefs.

77
00:02:47,190 --> 00:02:48,474
The goal was spelled out.

78
00:02:48,814 --> 00:02:51,070
A build-up of incidents that would place

79
00:02:51,090 --> 00:02:53,460
the United States in the apparent position

80
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,851
of suffering defensible grievances, from a

81
00:02:55,871 --> 00:02:58,241
rash and irresponsible government of Cuba.

82
00:02:58,811 --> 00:03:00,223
There was a time limit, too.

83
00:03:00,563 --> 00:03:02,802
The report said the plan would only hold

84
00:03:02,822 --> 00:03:05,004
up as long as an intervention would not

85
00:03:05,024 --> 00:03:06,924
directly involve the Soviet Union.

86
00:03:07,264 --> 00:03:09,144
So everything was meant to happen within

87
00:03:09,164 --> 00:03:10,094
the next few months.

88
00:03:10,664 --> 00:03:11,980
And it was tightly held.

89
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:14,881
The report recommended that the paper not

90
00:03:14,901 --> 00:03:17,461
go to the military's unified commands, to

91
00:03:17,481 --> 00:03:19,790
U.S. officers at NATO, or to the U.S.

92
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:21,993
delegation on the UN Military Staff

93
00:03:22,013 --> 00:03:22,622
Committee.

94
00:03:23,192 --> 00:03:25,248
An attached page quoted the Joint Chiefs

95
00:03:25,268 --> 00:03:26,337
from the week before.

96
00:03:26,677 --> 00:03:29,221
If a credible revolt inside Cuba proved

97
00:03:29,241 --> 00:03:31,915
impossible in the next nine to 10 months,

98
00:03:31,935 --> 00:03:34,347
that would require a U.S. decision to

99
00:03:34,367 --> 00:03:36,385
develop a Cuban provocation, as

100
00:03:36,405 --> 00:03:37,305
justification.

101
00:03:38,125 --> 00:03:39,350
So what was on the list?

102
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:42,304
The annex lays out nine courses of action.

103
00:03:42,644 --> 00:03:44,905
The first is a cover and deception plan,

104
00:03:44,925 --> 00:03:46,445
to provoke Cuban reactions.

105
00:03:46,785 --> 00:03:49,545
The second focuses on the U.S. naval base

106
00:03:49,565 --> 00:03:52,326
at Guantanamo Bay, on Cuba's southeastern

107
00:03:52,346 --> 00:03:52,597
tip.

108
00:03:53,167 --> 00:03:54,104
Start rumors.

109
00:03:54,444 --> 00:03:56,875
Land friendly Cubans, in uniform, over the

110
00:03:56,895 --> 00:03:59,093
fence, to stage an attack on the base.

111
00:03:59,433 --> 00:04:01,165
Start riots near the main gate.

112
00:04:01,735 --> 00:04:03,685
Blow up ammunition inside the base.

113
00:04:04,025 --> 00:04:04,941
Burn aircraft.

114
00:04:05,281 --> 00:04:07,210
Lob mortar shells in from outside.

115
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:09,824
Sink a ship near the harbor entrance, and

116
00:04:09,844 --> 00:04:11,620
conduct funerals for mock victims.

117
00:04:12,189 --> 00:04:14,587
Then the United States would respond, and

118
00:04:14,607 --> 00:04:17,004
in the memo's words, commence large scale

119
00:04:17,024 --> 00:04:19,009
United States military operations.

120
00:04:19,829 --> 00:04:21,827
The next idea borrowed from history.

121
00:04:22,167 --> 00:04:25,273
In 1898, the battleship USS Maine exploded

122
00:04:25,293 --> 00:04:26,539
in Havana harbor.

123
00:04:26,879 --> 00:04:28,845
266 men died.

124
00:04:29,415 --> 00:04:31,563
Remember the Maine became a rallying cry

125
00:04:31,583 --> 00:04:32,592
for war with Spain.

126
00:04:33,062 --> 00:04:35,307
Even though a later Navy study found the

127
00:04:35,327 --> 00:04:37,572
explosion most likely started inside the

128
00:04:37,592 --> 00:04:37,855
ship.

129
00:04:38,425 --> 00:04:40,619
The memo proposed a Remember the Maine

130
00:04:40,639 --> 00:04:41,143
incident.

131
00:04:41,726 --> 00:04:44,244
We could blow up a U.S. ship in Guantanamo

132
00:04:44,264 --> 00:04:45,996
Bay, it says, and blame Cuba.

133
00:04:46,566 --> 00:04:49,011
Or blow up an unmanned vessel near Havana,

134
00:04:49,031 --> 00:04:51,359
and stage a rescue for a crew that never

135
00:04:51,379 --> 00:04:51,828
existed.

136
00:04:52,298 --> 00:04:53,123
And then this.

137
00:04:53,694 --> 00:04:56,183
Casualty lists in U.S. newspapers would

138
00:04:56,203 --> 00:04:58,242
cause a helpful wave of national

139
00:04:58,262 --> 00:04:59,015
indignation.

140
00:05:00,035 --> 00:05:02,247
The next idea moved to American soil.

141
00:05:02,587 --> 00:05:05,030
A Communist Cuban terror campaign, in the

142
00:05:05,050 --> 00:05:07,432
Miami area, in other Florida cities, and

143
00:05:07,452 --> 00:05:08,574
even in Washington.

144
00:05:09,144 --> 00:05:11,283
Sink a boatload of Cubans headed for

145
00:05:11,303 --> 00:05:12,902
Florida, real or simulated.

146
00:05:13,242 --> 00:05:15,457
Foster attempts on the lives of Cuban

147
00:05:15,477 --> 00:05:17,993
refugees in the U.S., even to the point of

148
00:05:18,013 --> 00:05:18,537
wounding.

149
00:05:18,877 --> 00:05:21,357
Explode a few plastic bombs, in carefully

150
00:05:21,377 --> 00:05:22,150
chosen spots.

151
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:24,585
There were ideas for the sky, too.

152
00:05:24,925 --> 00:05:27,265
Harassment of civil air by U.S. pilots

153
00:05:27,285 --> 00:05:28,694
flying MiG-type planes.

154
00:05:29,034 --> 00:05:31,843
An F-86, painted to look like a Cuban MiG.

155
00:05:32,413 --> 00:05:34,602
One of the most detailed plans is number

156
00:05:34,622 --> 00:05:34,934
eight.

157
00:05:35,274 --> 00:05:37,621
A charter airliner, flying from the U.S.

158
00:05:37,641 --> 00:05:39,989
on a route over Cuba, would appear to be

159
00:05:40,009 --> 00:05:41,587
shot down by a Cuban plane.

160
00:05:41,927 --> 00:05:44,053
The passengers, the memo suggests, could

161
00:05:44,073 --> 00:05:46,146
be a group of college students off on a

162
00:05:46,166 --> 00:05:46,576
holiday.

163
00:05:47,146 --> 00:05:48,355
Here's how it would work.

164
00:05:48,695 --> 00:05:51,002
At Eglin Air Force Base in Florida, a

165
00:05:51,022 --> 00:05:53,140
plane would be painted as an exact

166
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:55,656
duplicate of a civil aircraft owned by a

167
00:05:55,676 --> 00:05:57,355
CIA front company in Miami.

168
00:05:57,924 --> 00:06:00,249
The duplicate would carry the passengers,

169
00:06:00,269 --> 00:06:01,736
all boarded under aliases.

170
00:06:02,076 --> 00:06:04,399
South of Florida, it would drop to minimum

171
00:06:04,419 --> 00:06:06,743
altitude and land at an auxiliary field at

172
00:06:06,763 --> 00:06:07,077
Eglin.

173
00:06:07,547 --> 00:06:09,548
The real plane, converted to a drone,

174
00:06:09,568 --> 00:06:10,585
would fly on alone.

175
00:06:11,155 --> 00:06:13,370
Over Cuba, the drone would broadcast a

176
00:06:13,390 --> 00:06:15,840
MAYDAY call, saying it was under attack by

177
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:16,487
Cuban MiGs.

178
00:06:16,907 --> 00:06:18,893
Then it would be destroyed by radio

179
00:06:18,913 --> 00:06:19,294
signal.

180
00:06:19,865 --> 00:06:21,090
The memo's reasoning?

181
00:06:21,610 --> 00:06:23,731
International aviation radio stations

182
00:06:23,751 --> 00:06:26,162
would tell the U.S. what happened, instead

183
00:06:26,182 --> 00:06:28,478
of the U.S. trying to sell the incident.

184
00:06:29,047 --> 00:06:31,203
Pretext number nine faked the loss of an

185
00:06:31,223 --> 00:06:32,128
American fighter.

186
00:06:32,468 --> 00:06:35,030
Four or five F-101 jets would fly from

187
00:06:35,050 --> 00:06:37,544
Homestead Air Force Base toward Cuba.

188
00:06:38,114 --> 00:06:40,211
One pre-briefed pilot would radio that

189
00:06:40,231 --> 00:06:42,272
MiGs had jumped him, and he was going

190
00:06:42,292 --> 00:06:42,550
down.

191
00:06:42,890 --> 00:06:45,021
Then he'd fly low to a secure base, and

192
00:06:45,041 --> 00:06:47,117
the plane would get a new tail number.

193
00:06:47,687 --> 00:06:50,036
Meanwhile, a submarine or small boat would

194
00:06:50,056 --> 00:06:52,405
scatter aircraft parts and a parachute off

195
00:06:52,425 --> 00:06:54,773
the Cuban coast, for search ships to find.

196
00:06:55,694 --> 00:06:57,020
So what happened to the list?

197
00:06:57,640 --> 00:07:00,045
On March 16, three days after the memo,

198
00:07:00,065 --> 00:07:02,160
President Kennedy met with his top

199
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:03,217
advisers on Cuba.

200
00:07:03,557 --> 00:07:05,139
General Lemnitzer was there.

201
00:07:05,709 --> 00:07:07,748
According to a note of that meeting by

202
00:07:07,768 --> 00:07:09,265
State Department official U.

203
00:07:09,605 --> 00:07:11,635
Alexis Johnson, the president was

204
00:07:11,655 --> 00:07:14,119
skeptical that circumstances would arise

205
00:07:14,139 --> 00:07:16,727
to justify using American forces for overt

206
00:07:16,747 --> 00:07:17,720
military action.

207
00:07:18,291 --> 00:07:20,339
The note adds that no decision was

208
00:07:20,359 --> 00:07:22,834
expressed or implied approving the use of

209
00:07:22,854 --> 00:07:23,564
such forces.

210
00:07:23,984 --> 00:07:25,966
Contingency planning would go on.

211
00:07:26,536 --> 00:07:27,446
One caution.

212
00:07:27,786 --> 00:07:29,816
The released record doesn't show exactly

213
00:07:29,836 --> 00:07:31,815
how much of the Northwoods list reached

214
00:07:31,835 --> 00:07:32,942
the president himself.

215
00:07:33,512 --> 00:07:36,115
Reporting on the files in 2001, ABC News

216
00:07:36,135 --> 00:07:38,344
said the plans had apparently been

217
00:07:38,364 --> 00:07:40,705
rejected by the civilian leadership.

218
00:07:41,175 --> 00:07:43,256
And no released record shows any of these

219
00:07:43,276 --> 00:07:44,640
pretexts being carried out.

220
00:07:45,210 --> 00:07:47,286
That fall, Lemnitzer's term as Chairman

221
00:07:47,306 --> 00:07:47,608
ended.

222
00:07:47,948 --> 00:07:49,611
Kennedy did not reappoint him.

223
00:07:49,951 --> 00:07:52,971
In January 1963, he became NATO's Supreme

224
00:07:52,991 --> 00:07:54,973
Allied Commander in Europe.

225
00:07:55,543 --> 00:07:57,694
The Joint Chiefs' official biography of

226
00:07:57,714 --> 00:07:59,920
Lemnitzer does not connect that decision

227
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:00,699
to Northwoods.

228
00:08:01,039 --> 00:08:03,010
It does not mention Northwoods at all.

229
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:06,371
And in October 1962, the month Lansdale's

230
00:08:06,391 --> 00:08:08,907
schedule had picked for a revolt, the

231
00:08:08,927 --> 00:08:10,757
Cuban missile crisis began.

232
00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:13,819
The memo's own condition, an intervention

233
00:08:13,839 --> 00:08:16,074
without direct Soviet involvement, no

234
00:08:16,094 --> 00:08:16,805
longer held.

235
00:08:17,725 --> 00:08:20,002
For decades, the memo sat in classified

236
00:08:20,022 --> 00:08:21,121
Joint Chiefs files.

237
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:23,738
It came out because of a different effort.

238
00:08:24,078 --> 00:08:27,276
In 1992, Congress passed the JFK Records

239
00:08:27,296 --> 00:08:27,597
Act.

240
00:08:27,937 --> 00:08:30,025
It created an independent panel, the

241
00:08:30,045 --> 00:08:32,251
Assassination Records Review Board, to

242
00:08:32,271 --> 00:08:34,593
release records connected to the Kennedy

243
00:08:34,613 --> 00:08:35,412
assassination.

244
00:08:35,983 --> 00:08:37,416
The Board's net was wide.

245
00:08:37,756 --> 00:08:40,060
According to a draft of its final report,

246
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:42,384
about two out of every three Joint Chiefs

247
00:08:42,404 --> 00:08:44,424
records it collected were about Cuba

248
00:08:44,444 --> 00:08:44,821
policy.

249
00:08:45,391 --> 00:08:47,952
In October 1997, the Board took up a

250
00:08:47,972 --> 00:08:50,676
related Joint Chiefs memo, from August

251
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:53,328
1962, on proposed military operations

252
00:08:53,348 --> 00:08:56,124
against Cuba and the justifications for

253
00:08:56,144 --> 00:08:56,483
them.

254
00:08:56,823 --> 00:08:58,909
According to a Board letter, NSC and

255
00:08:58,929 --> 00:09:01,132
Defense Department reviewers raised no

256
00:09:01,152 --> 00:09:03,471
objection, and the Joint Staff agreed to

257
00:09:03,491 --> 00:09:05,402
release it with minor redactions.

258
00:09:05,972 --> 00:09:08,910
The Northwoods case file, 197 pages, is

259
00:09:08,930 --> 00:09:11,488
part of the National Archives' JFK

260
00:09:11,508 --> 00:09:12,322
collection.

261
00:09:12,892 --> 00:09:15,354
It reached a wide audience in 2001, when

262
00:09:15,374 --> 00:09:17,836
author James Bamford described it in his

263
00:09:17,856 --> 00:09:20,255
book, Body of Secrets, and the National

264
00:09:20,275 --> 00:09:22,736
Security Archive posted the memo online.

265
00:09:23,306 --> 00:09:25,335
Bamford wrote that it may be the most

266
00:09:25,355 --> 00:09:27,383
corrupt plan ever created by the U.S.

267
00:09:27,403 --> 00:09:27,992
government.

268
00:09:28,462 --> 00:09:29,597
That's his judgment.

269
00:09:29,937 --> 00:09:32,132
The document itself is a planning memo.

270
00:09:32,952 --> 00:09:34,977
So, what does this file actually prove?

271
00:09:35,597 --> 00:09:38,009
It proves that in 1962, the Joint Chiefs

272
00:09:38,029 --> 00:09:40,259
of Staff put staged attacks on paper,

273
00:09:40,279 --> 00:09:42,629
endorsed them as a preliminary planning

274
00:09:42,649 --> 00:09:45,183
submission, and sent them to the Secretary

275
00:09:45,203 --> 00:09:45,851
of Defense.

276
00:09:46,422 --> 00:09:48,426
Some of the ideas would have put real

277
00:09:48,446 --> 00:09:49,247
